[01:30] [scene:result]
VISUAL: Wide shot of a stadium with people sitting in the stands and on the field.
AUDIO: 'to film myself without people noticing. One of the easiest ones is just taking my phone and placing the camera right in front of it. On top of blending in, this also helps keep the camera steady when'

[01:42] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'stabilization is turned off. And I like having the option to record shaky or smooth footage. Like when your country is about to score in the World Cup but can\'t finish.'

[01:54] [scene:result]
VISUAL: Exterior shot of a stadium entrance gate.
AUDIO: 'That chaos of the crowd is captured through camera shakes. &gt;&gt; Oh, god damn it. &gt;&gt; We lost. &gt;&gt; Or when you lose that football match and leave the stadium, a smooth camera move captures the melancholy of the moment.'

[02:06] [scene:intro]
VISUAL: Creator walking through a shopping mall, holding the camera.
AUDIO: '&gt;&gt; Of course, none of that footage matters if the audio is bad. And there are a lot of ways to record your voice while vlogging, but very few of them are invisible. What I like to do is camouflage the'

[02:18] [scene:demo]
VISUAL: Creator holding a Sharpie, demonstrating blacking out a microphone clip.
AUDIO: 'microphone into my outfit. And you can do this by choosing clothes with natural folds, like a jacket collar or suspenders on overalls, and then placing the mic in the right'

[02:30] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'spot so that the clip looks like a little pin. And then you can use a Sharpie to black out any logos on that clip. Like that. See? Much better.'

